message: "If you use FractalFlow, please cite the software release and the accompanying technical report."
title: "FractalFlow: Deep-Zoom Julia Set Explorer"
type: software
version: 1.1.0
date-released: 2026-07-28
authors:
  - given-names: Timofei
    family-names: Amosov
abstract: >-
  FractalFlow is an interactive deep-zoom Julia set explorer implementing
  perturbation rendering across WebGPU/WGSL and native CUDA, with a WebGL2
  compatibility backend and independent arbitrary-precision validation.
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/Timmor77/FractalFlow"
url: "https://timmor77.github.io/FractalFlow/"
keywords:
  - Julia set
  - deep zoom
  - perturbation theory
  - WebGPU
  - WGSL
  - CUDA
  - double-double arithmetic
  - numerical validation
